What is a Supplier?

Supplier is part of java.util.function package.
It does not take any input
It returns (supplies) a value of type T
So, it’s the opposite of Consumer.
get() is the abstract method

| Concept         | Description                                                   |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Supplier**    | A functional interface that **supplies** values without input |
| **Method**      | `T get()`                                                     |
| **Common Uses** | Generate randoms, default values, lazy initialization         |
| **Analogy**     | 🥤 Vending machine — you don’t give input, it gives output    |
| **In Streams**  | Used with `Stream.generate()`                                 |


import java.util.function.Supplier;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class SupplierStreamExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Supplier<Double> randomSupplier = () -> Math.random();

        Stream.generate(randomSupplier)  // Infinite stream of random numbers
              .limit(5)                  // Take only first 5
              .forEach(System.out::println);  // Print each
    }
}
